    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. we've been running some automated tests but we're still seeing some weird, inconsistent glitches where certain elements aren't being announced or the colors look off on some specific devices. it feels like these little bugs are just lurking in the code and popping up randomly. any tips on how to track down those kinds of sneaky issues during an audit?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sneaky issues like those are often the result of poor state management or unexpected rendering paths, which is why you need a more hands-on approach than just automated tools. You should employ manual testing, specifically using a combination of browser developer tools and real user devices. For the announcement glitches, try stepping through the DOM structure with the accessibility inspector in your browser while the screen reader is active. This helps you see *what* the screen reader is actually reading versus *what* you intended it to read.",
      "source": "target",
